Provide Sonos Radio Service
When you use Sonos Radio service, we collect and process certain Functional Data (e.g., your IP address, language selection, your Sonos ID, radio stations browsing history, your search terms for stations, playback actions, system, third party device ID and type, and content events such as individual radio stations and/or tracks), location data, age, gender and other listening activity (e.g., listening session length, stations listened to, and tracks listened to and skipped) within Sonos Radio. We collect and process this information in order to provide you with a customized experience, respond to your requests, provide the requested service to you, to determine relevant licensing obligations, to serve marketing communications, for advertising purposes and to improve Sonos Products and Services.
Additionally, when you use the free, advertising-supported version of Sonos Radio, we collect and may share the following categories of data with our advertising service providers and advertising partners for the purpose of delivering, managing, and optimizing advertisements:
Identifiers:
your IP address from which your device accesses the Sonos app or service;
HTTP user agent and HTTP referer information (when available);
information that may be used for device recognition (device fingerprinting);
geolocation data derived from your IP address (GeoIP);
your consent or opt-out preferences;
your email address in hashed form, used to generate pseudonymous advertising identifiers;
pseudonymous advertising identifiers, such as Unified ID 2.0 (UID2),, or equivalent industry identifiers;
mobile advertising identifiers assigned to your device, such as Apple's Identifier for Advertisers (IDFA) or Google's Advertising ID (AAID), where available and where you have not opted out through your device settings (including iOS tracking permissions or Android advertising settings);
Non-precise location data made available by your player or device (where you have not opted out of location sharing);
Demographic information:
age range and gender, where available;
Listening context:
the genre of the station you are currently listening to, podcast title, duration of play, advertisement impression timestamps, your language preference, and your Sonos ID;
Advertising engagement data: impression triggers, the identifiers of the advertising creatives served to you, completion rates, and frequency-capping records.
This data is used for the following advertising-related purposes: delivering advertisements; measuring advertisement performance; limiting the number of times you see a particular advertisement (frequency capping); preventing advertising fraud; enforcing geographic content restrictions (e.g., broadcast blackouts and music licensing limits), determining relevant licensing obligations and requirements to performance rights organizations, reporting to advertisers; and audience targeting and advertisement optimization.
Your IP address and an anonymized ID will continue to be provided to third-party radio content providers to provide you with access to radio stations.
Demographic and interest-based information about you will be received from third-party data providers, which advertising service providers use to select relevant advertisements for you.
This processing is necessary for the performance of our agreement with you, as well as to serve our legitimate interest. Where applicable law provides you with the right to opt out of targeted advertising or the “sale” or “sharing” of your personal information (including under the CCPA and other US state privacy laws), you may exercise those rights as described in the “Your Rights and Choices” section and the California Addendum below. For more information on this, please visit
The Legal Bases for Using Personal Information
.
